-- 0878 · The faith demo: the community member finds a full, lived-in app (owner request 2026-10-16: "the community member persona: fill up all spots that
-- we can fill with test data; where we don't have data, take a few examples from the real community and copy them over so the experience is full").
--
-- Pack demo_faith_jain_v1 goes to version 6. The persona is Tarun Patni (the family's main adult; Nisha is his wife; Dev 9, Maya 8 and Aarav 5 are in the Learning
-- Center). Before this, most screens of the member app were empty or thin for him. Every row below is invented; the kinds of things (a Sunday times table, a dinner
-- with donation choices, class announcements, a feedback form after an event, building-fund style giving choices) follow the earlier community pack (0312)
-- and the structure of the real community's content, with every word reworded for a house of worship that is not any one faith (the generator stops on a tradition's
-- word) and no real person's name, phone, e-mail, address or link. Photo albums link to a placeholder address on a domain nobody owns.
--
--   Money      Two pledges and three payments of the Patni family, in whole cents: the annual appeal ($100.00) paid in full by check (receipt SUNRISE WORSHIP DEMO-R-...),
--              and a row of bricks for the new hall ($500.00) paid in part ($200.00 by Zelle, $100.00 by a test-mode card payment), so the family has one paid pledge
--              and one partly paid pledge, with receipts. Their open pledges are untouched: the $51.00 general pledge is still open with no payment against it (an
--              unmatched $51.00 Zelle bank line waits for it) and so are the three Learning Center fee pledges. The new part-paid pledge is NEWER than the oldest
--              of them, so the pledge the demo hangs a waiting payment confirmation on (0877: the family's oldest open pledge with at least $25.00 open) is the same as before.
--              Five things to give to (Founding circle, Pillar sponsor, Brick by brick with three choices, Any amount for the new hall, Sponsor a shared meal) and a
--              monthly gift of $25.00 that waits for a card and is never charged.
--   Store      Two orders of the family: one picked up last time, one placed for the next pickup (items that are not counted on the shelf, so the low-stock list is unchanged).
--   Events     The appreciation dinner gets a shared meal in six lunch times and donation choices on the RSVP; a weekly gathering tomorrow morning (36 hours' notice,
--              so "Still coming?" waits for the family all day); the family attended the last weekly gathering.
--   Calendar   Two layers (gatherings and events, Learning Center), entries for every published event and the Learning Center's days; two photo albums (links);
--              an event-feedback form for the last gathering (open) and an open poll, with a few answers.
--   Guide      The pages the Life tiles open: Times and visiting (a | What | When | table, also read by Home), Links, Membership. A question the front office
--              answered and closed (shows in the family's messages), the committee lists, library texts the assistant answers from, two published texts.
--   Family     Four special days, a request to add a grandparent (for the membership coordinator), profile details with an emergency contact, the family's member
--              numbers, and whether each adult may vote (not yet: the yearly application is with the membership team).
--   Learning   For the class the three children attend: four class days with attendance, two published progress reports, three class announcements, a learning path
--     Center   of the community's own ("Kindness at home": two levels of three steps, with the children's progress) and an open place to volunteer as a teacher.
--
-- NOT HERE, AND WHY. Statements (a tax-year PDF in storage), photos and videos (files in storage), audio and video lessons (media files) and the day's
-- timings table (its columns are one tradition's) cannot be loaded by a pack, or would speak a tradition; those screens stay thin. The class days are the dates
-- of the last weeks, not Sundays: a pack's dates are relative to today.
--
-- THE LIVE DEMO. A migration changes the pack; the running community reloads it by itself (0877: the pack is part of the demo's fingerprint, so the next hourly
-- check reloads it), or at once with Platform > Setup > Demo sign-in > Start over. This migration also runs app.demo_align_center and writes one audit entry
-- ("demo.pack_updated") for every faith demo community still on an older pack, as 0840 did. No policy, grant, permission or money rule of any object is changed.

